{{wikipedia}}
{{was wotd|2012|January|11}}
===Etymology===
From {{etyl|fr}} {{term|pétiole}}, and its source, {{etyl|la}} {{term|petiolus||little foot}}, diminuitive form of {{term|pes}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ˈpɛtɪəʊl/}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|/ˈpɛdiˌoʊl/}}, {{X-SAMPA|/"pEti%oUl/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{botany}} The [[stalk]] of a [[leaf]], attaching the [[blade]] to the [[stem]].
# {{entomology}} A narrow or constricted [[segment]] of the body of an [[insect]]. Used especially to refer to the [[metasomal]] segment of [[Hymenoptera]] such as wasps.
# {{entomology}} The stalk at the base of the nest of the [[paper wasp]].

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|segment of the body of an insect}} [[pedicel]]

====Derived terms====
* [[petiolar]]
* [[petiolary]]

